@baseUrl = http://localhost:5170
@admin = admin
@from = 2026-11-01T00:00:00Z
@to = 2026-11-30T00:00:00Z

# Run the sample first:  dotnet run --project samples/ChronoAudit.Sample.WebApi
# The demo sign-in is the header X-Demo-User. The sample gives every demo user the All scope.
# The activity log and the audit search accept a range of at most 31 days (366 when you also name a user, a session, an actor or a record). Move the dates to cover your calls.

### ------------------------------------------------------------
### 1. The demo domain (/books): every call below is audited,
###    logged, and the writes record a mutation intent and a timeline event
### ------------------------------------------------------------

### List books
GET {{baseUrl}}/books
X-Demo-User: {{admin}}

### Create a book
# @name createBook
POST {{baseUrl}}/books
X-Demo-User: {{admin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "Dune", "isbn": "9780441172719", "author": "Frank Herbert" }

### Change it
PUT {{baseUrl}}/books/1
X-Demo-User: {{admin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "Dune (revised)", "author": "Frank Herbert" }

### Delete it (a soft delete: the row stays, IsDeleted becomes true)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/books/1
X-Demo-User: {{admin}}

### ------------------------------------------------------------
### 2. History: /chronoaudit/history (All scope)
### ------------------------------------------------------------

### Modules and tables that can be read
GET {{baseUrl}}/chronoaudit/history/tables
X-Demo-User: {{admin}}

### Changes of a table
GET {{baseUrl}}/chronoaudit/history/library/tables/Books/changes?limit=20
X-Demo-User: {{admin}}

### Changes of one record
GET {{baseUrl}}/chronoaudit/history/library/tables/Books/records/1/changes
X-Demo-User: {{admin}}

### ------------------------------------------------------------
### 3. Audit trail: /chronoaudit/audit (All scope)
### ------------------------------------------------------------

### Search raw audit rows (from and to are required)
GET {{baseUrl}}/chronoaudit/audit/library/search?from={{from}}&to={{to}}&limit=20
X-Demo-User: {{admin}}

### Re-walk the hash chain of a module
POST {{baseUrl}}/chronoaudit/audit/verify
X-Demo-User: {{admin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "module": "library" }

### Verify the activity-log chain
POST {{baseUrl}}/chronoaudit/audit/verify
X-Demo-User: {{admin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "module": "chronoaudit-activity" }

### ------------------------------------------------------------
### 4. Activity log: /chronoaudit/activity
### ------------------------------------------------------------

### Search API calls
GET {{baseUrl}}/chronoaudit/activity/search?from={{from}}&to={{to}}&limit=20
X-Demo-User: {{admin}}

### Only failed calls
GET {{baseUrl}}/chronoaudit/activity/search?from={{from}}&to={{to}}&statusClass=4xx
X-Demo-User: {{admin}}

### Calls per day (by = day, month, endpoint, statusClass or user)
GET {{baseUrl}}/chronoaudit/activity/statistics?from={{from}}&to={{to}}&by=day
X-Demo-User: {{admin}}

### Download the calls as CSV
GET {{baseUrl}}/chronoaudit/activity/export.csv?from={{from}}&to={{to}}
X-Demo-User: {{admin}}

### Write requests that arrived and never got a result
GET {{baseUrl}}/chronoaudit/activity/intents/incomplete
X-Demo-User: {{admin}}

### The masked body of one call (use an id from the search; the view is audited)
GET {{baseUrl}}/chronoaudit/activity/requests/1/body
X-Demo-User: {{admin}}

### ------------------------------------------------------------
### 5. Analytics: /chronoaudit/analytics
### ------------------------------------------------------------

### What can be analyzed
GET {{baseUrl}}/chronoaudit/analytics/catalog
X-Demo-User: {{admin}}

### Calls by method
POST {{baseUrl}}/chronoaudit/analytics/run
X-Demo-User: {{admin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "subject": "activity",
  "dimensions": [ "method" ],
  "measures": [ "count", "avgDurationMs" ],
  "from": "2026-11-01T00:00:00Z",
  "to": "2026-11-30T00:00:00Z"
}

### ------------------------------------------------------------
### 6. Saved reports: /chronoaudit/saved-reports
### ------------------------------------------------------------

### Save a report
# @name createReport
POST {{baseUrl}}/chronoaudit/saved-reports
X-Demo-User: {{admin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Calls by method",
  "definition": {
    "subject": "activity",
    "dimensions": [ "method" ],
    "measures": [ "count" ],
    "from": "2026-11-01T00:00:00Z",
    "to": "2026-11-30T00:00:00Z"
  }
}

###
@reportId = {{createReport.response.body.$.id}}
@stamp = {{createReport.response.body.$.concurrencyStamp}}

### List reports
GET {{baseUrl}}/chronoaudit/saved-reports
X-Demo-User: {{admin}}

### Read one
GET {{baseUrl}}/chronoaudit/saved-reports/{{reportId}}
X-Demo-User: {{admin}}

### Run it over another period
POST {{baseUrl}}/chronoaudit/saved-reports/{{reportId}}/run
X-Demo-User: {{admin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "from": "2026-11-01T00:00:00Z", "to": "2026-11-30T00:00:00Z" }

### Delete it (the stamp protects against deleting a report someone changed)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/chronoaudit/saved-reports/{{reportId}}?expectedStamp={{stamp}}
X-Demo-User: {{admin}}

### ------------------------------------------------------------
### 7. Exports: /chronoaudit/exports
### ------------------------------------------------------------

### Ask for an export (producers: activity, audit, extract, analytics, timeline)
# @name createExport
POST {{baseUrl}}/chronoaudit/exports
X-Demo-User: {{admin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "producer": "activity",
  "format": "Csv",
  "parameters": { "from": "2026-11-01T00:00:00Z", "to": "2026-11-30T00:00:00Z" }
}

###
@exportId = {{createExport.response.body.$.id}}

### My jobs
GET {{baseUrl}}/chronoaudit/exports?limit=10
X-Demo-User: {{admin}}

### One job (wait for state Completed)
GET {{baseUrl}}/chronoaudit/exports/{{exportId}}
X-Demo-User: {{admin}}

### Download the file (the header X-Content-SHA256 holds its hash)
GET {{baseUrl}}/chronoaudit/exports/{{exportId}}/download
X-Demo-User: {{admin}}

### Cancel a job that has not finished
POST {{baseUrl}}/chronoaudit/exports/{{exportId}}/cancel
X-Demo-User: {{admin}}

### ------------------------------------------------------------
### 8. Extract: /chronoaudit/extract (All scope)
### ------------------------------------------------------------

### Stream the audit rows of all modules as CSV
GET {{baseUrl}}/chronoaudit/extract/csv?from={{from}}&to={{to}}&includeTimeline=true
X-Demo-User: {{admin}}

### ------------------------------------------------------------
### 9. Timeline: /chronoaudit/timeline
### ------------------------------------------------------------

### Events of a subject
GET {{baseUrl}}/chronoaudit/timeline/subjects/Book/1?limit=20
X-Demo-User: {{admin}}

### Events of a group (the demo uses the book id)
GET {{baseUrl}}/chronoaudit/timeline/groups/1?limit=20
X-Demo-User: {{admin}}

### Events a user took part in
GET {{baseUrl}}/chronoaudit/timeline/actors/admin?limit=20
X-Demo-User: {{admin}}

### Evidence bundle of a record (All scope; issuing it is audited first). SubjectType is the audit table name, SubjectId the record id.
GET {{baseUrl}}/chronoaudit/timeline/subjects/Books/1/evidence
X-Demo-User: {{admin}}
